 	    "visible; stage 1 status 2: this Data store has no capture plug-in)\n", source, point, oneios_camera_addon_stage,
 	    oneios_camera_addon_status);
 }
+/*
+ * OneiOS (0091): OneiOS's own apps (2048, Bench) in /Applications. The registrar oneios-appreg (userland/apps) keeps a copy
+ * of its bundles in the Data folder /private/var/oneios/appsview; shown here over /Applications as a read-only union, above
+ * 0035's view of the staged system apps (that one is taken while /private/var is still the OS volume's, so a bundle copied
+ * to the Data volume's /private/var/staged_system_apps is never seen: take22). The registrar cannot mount this itself: the
+ * platform sandbox profile refuses any process's mount there (take23 on the phone: errno 1, a sandbox violation for the
+ * file-mount in iOS's log), while the boot mounts of this file are the kernel's. Stage 5: an app of the sealed
+ * /Applications (Settings) and one of the staged view (Weather) are still found through it; a view that is mounted and
+ * hides one of them is taken off again at once. Before 0037's and 0043's look at the LaunchServices store, so the store
+ * that does not name the two bundles yet is dropped once and lsd registers them with the other system apps.
+ * oneios-apps-view=0 turns it off. A Data store without the folder (the registrar makes it at its first run): stage 1,
+ * status 2, and the view comes at the next boot.
+ */
+static volatile int oneios_own_apps_stage = 0;
+static volatile int oneios_own_apps_status = -1;
+static void
+oneios_own_apps_view(proc_t p, user_addr_t scratch)
+{
+	static const char source[] = "/private/var/oneios/appsview", point[] = "/Applications";
+	uint32_t enabled = 1;
+	PE_parse_boot_argn("oneios-apps-view", &enabled, sizeof(enabled));
+	if (enabled == 0) {
+		printf("oneios-apps-view: off (oneios-apps-view=0)\n");
+		return;
+	}
+	/* Scratch 0xa00..0xb20: 0056's mount above has returned (0081's, later, uses it after this one). */
+	native_gpu_addon_mount(p, scratch, 0xa00, source, sizeof(source), point, sizeof(point),
+	    "/Applications/Preferences.app/Info.plist", "/Applications/Weather.app/Info.plist", &oneios_own_apps_stage,
+	    &oneios_own_apps_status);
+	int undone = -1;
+	if (oneios_own_apps_stage == 3 || oneios_own_apps_stage == 4) {
+		/* mounted, and Settings or Weather is not found through it: off again (the point's path is still in the scratch) */
+		struct unmount_args undo = {.path = scratch + 0xa00 + 0x20, .flags = MNT_FORCE};
+		int32_t result = 0;
+		undone = unmount(p, &undo, &result);
+	}
+	printf("oneios-apps-view: %s over %s: stage %d, status %d (stage 5 status 0: mounted, Settings and Weather still visible "
+	    "below it; stage 1 status 2: no such folder yet)%s\n", source, point, oneios_own_apps_stage, oneios_own_apps_status,
+	    undone == 0 ? "; taken off again" : undone > 0 ? "; NOT taken off (unmount failed)" : "");
+}
 #endif
 #if XNU_HOSTED || XNU_ONEIOS_NATIVE
